{"title":"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is right-angled at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/0989b5e597cbb93095b7004ecf4f96b43c6fc40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/5369aff2ec3a2e0a3604e4ba2b6a7fa3c3e2bc6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Originally, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/e/1ae1fcd46985ba5f87bb9acecda68b9e5b9390c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{24^{2} + 10^{2}} = \\sqrt{576 + 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"259\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/a/d9a3e1fd84438d5426275c349ce75f7c64541793.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sqrt{676} = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>We could have also realized that the triangle's sides are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times that of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b366d6db9da6fcb54728dda03541ec577b4cc000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 13 \\times 2 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Next, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> are increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, their new values are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.\n</p><p>The new value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/9/339defbb614cfbd951a3556bdcf367aa86348acf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = \\sqrt{30^{2} + 16^{2}} = \\sqrt{900 + 256} = \\sqrt{1156} = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"377\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>We could have also realized that the triangle's sides are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times that of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle to find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/4152288ff0f2cbb3ca3875ae29fd21fd493f0a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 17 \\times 2 = 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8e390635bb47934a309b84ff1d86c37b50c559.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34 - 26 = \\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC\">2014 CEMC CTMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_2\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 2\">Team Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Team_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Team Problem 4 (page does not exist)\">Team Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_CTMC_Problems/Individual_Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC CTMC Problems/Individual Problem 1\